# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Second Brain: git tracks the PUBLIC ENGINE ONLY
#
#  Allowlist: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only the engine files.
#  Your raw/, wiki/, agents.md and anything else you create stay private
#  by default. You'd have to add them here on purpose to commit them.
#  (gitignore comments must sit on their own line, never after a pattern.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*

# Public engine (safe to share)
!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/package.json
!/docs/
!/prompts/
!/scripts/
!/templates/
!/example/

# ─── Private: listed explicitly as a second layer, in case the allowlist is ever removed ───
# your sources: voice dumps, CVs, exports (may contain logins!)
/raw/
# your compiled knowledge
/wiki/
# your personal operating manual + Claude Code pointer
/agents.md
/CLAUDE.md
# vault settings + recently opened files (reveal note names)
/.obsidian/
/example/.obsidian/
# wiki-bundle.md = your ENTIRE wiki in one file
/.kb/
/example/.kb/
# Obsidian's deleted notes
/.trash/
# Notion / Google / other exports
*.zip

# ─── Secrets: never commit, even inside allowed folders ───
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*secret*
*credential*
*password*
id_rsa*

# ─── Junk ───
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
